-- title:
--   Scaled truncations of the logarithm land in p^N R
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative ring, $p$ a prime such that $p$ is a non-zero-divisor in $\mathcal O$, with an $\mathcal O$-algebra structure on $\mathbb Z/p$ whose structure map has kernel $(p)$, and with $\mathcal O$ complete for the $(p)$-adic filtration. Let $F$ be a $d$-dimensional commutative formal group law over $\mathcal O$ (a $d$-tuple of power series in $X_{\mathrm{inl}},X_{\mathrm{inr}}$ with zero constant term, identity linear part, associative, and invariant under swapping the two groups of variables). Let $F_p$ be a $d$-tuple of power series in $2d$ variables with zero constant term satisfying $p\cdot\mathrm{coeff}_m(F_{p,i}) = p^{|m|}\,\mathrm{coeff}_m(F_i)$ for all $m \neq 0$, and let $\varphi$ be a $d$-tuple of power series in $d$ variables with zero constant term, linear part the identity matrix, coefficients tending $p$-adically to $0$ (for each $N$ and $i$, all but finitely many coefficients of $\varphi_i$ lie in $(p^N)$), and satisfying the additivity $\varphi_i \circ F_p = \varphi_i(X_{\mathrm{inl}}) + \varphi_i(X_{\mathrm{inr}})$. Let $v \in \mathbb N$ and let $R$ be a commutative $\mathcal O$-Hopf algebra, free and finite as an $\mathcal O$-module, with $R$ and $R \otimes_{\mathcal O} R$ complete for their $(p)$-adic filtrations. Let $\pi : \mathcal O[[X_1,\dots,X_d]] \to R$ be a surjective $\mathcal O$-algebra map such that each $\pi(X_i)$ lies in the radical of $(p)R$, such that $\pi$ is given on every power series by $(p)$-adic evaluation at the points $\pi(X_i)$ ([`MvFormalGroup.adicEval`](def/MvFormalGroup_PointsV2.html#L20)), whose kernel is the ideal generated by the $d$ components of the $p^v$-fold iterate $[p^v]_F$ defined by `F.nthSeries` ($0$ at stage $0$, and $F(\text{stage }n, X)$ at stage $n+1$), and such that the comultiplication of $R$ satisfies $\Delta(\pi(X_i)) = F_i\bigl(\pi(X_j)\otimes 1,\,1\otimes\pi(X_j)\bigr)$, evaluated $(p)$-adically in $R\otimes_{\mathcal O}R$. Assume finally that the Cartier dual of $\mathbb Z/p \otimes_{\mathcal O} R$, that is the $\mathbb Z/p$-linear dual [`CartierDual (ZMod p) (ZMod p ⊗ R)`](def/HopfAlgebra_CartierDual.html#L12) with its ring structure, is a local ring. Then there is $N_1$ such that for every $N \ge N_1$, every $i$, and every power series $G$ in $d$ variables over $\mathcal O$ whose coefficients satisfy: $\mathrm{coeff}_m(G) = p^{N-|m|}\,\mathrm{coeff}_m(\varphi_i)$ whenever $|m| \le N$, and for $|m| > N$ either $\mathrm{coeff}_m(G)\cdot p^{|m|-N} = \mathrm{coeff}_m(\varphi_i)$ or else $\mathrm{coeff}_m(G) = 0$ and $p^{|m|-N} \nmid \mathrm{coeff}_m(\varphi_i)$, one has $\pi(G) \in p^N R$.
--
--   This is the claim, in Conrad's analysis of finite flat group schemes over bases with low ramification, that the scaled truncations of the logarithm of a formal group law are killed modulo $p^N$ in the quotient $\mathcal O[[X]]/([p^v]_F)$, so that the logarithm covector lies in the kernel of Fontaine's map. It feeds the construction of Witt-vector ghost components in [`Deformation.exists_wittVector_ghostComponent_truncate_map_mem_wittHom_fontaineKer_of_mvFormalGroup`](thm.html#Deformation.exists_wittVector_ghostComponent_truncate_map_mem_wittHom_fontaineKer_of_mvFormalGroup), and its coefficient bookkeeping rests on [`MvFormalGroup.natCast_mul_coeff_add_single_mem_span_pow_degree_of_subst_rescale_eq_add`](thm.html#MvFormalGroup.natCast_mul_coeff_add_single_mem_span_pow_degree_of_subst_rescale_eq_add).
